IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-1984`
IMPORT `cat-act-facts`
IMPORT `cat-regulations-2012`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA), compilation 00-l0-01, currency start 25 Sep 2025 (mrdoc_48898).
-- Part 1 -- Preliminary: ss 2, 3 and 4. LQA run cat-act-2011-lqa, step 4A, 2026-10-01.
-- s 1 (short title) is not encoded (coverage.json).
--
-- Also here: the encoding's reading of "has reached N months of age" and "a child under 18
-- years of age", because ss 4, 5, 9, 14 and 18 all turn on it (FORK-01).

§ `Section 2 -- Commencement`

DECLARE `Provision of Parts 1 and 2` IS ONE OF
    `s 1`, `s 2`, `s 3`, `s 4`, `s 5`, `s 6`, `s 7`, `s 8`, `s 9`, `s 10`, `s 11`, `s 12`, `s 13`,
    `s 14(1)`, `s 14(2)-(3)`, `s 15`, `s 16`, `s 17`, `s 18(1)`, `s 18(2)-(3)`, `s 19`, `s 20`,
    `s 21`, `s 22`, `s 23`, `s 24`, `s 25`

-- s 2: "This Act comes into operation as follows — (a) sections 1 and 2 — on the day on which
-- this Act receives the Royal Assent; (b) the rest of the Act, other than the provisions
-- referred to in paragraph (c) — on 1 November 2012; (c) sections 5, 6, 14(1), 18(1), 22 to
-- 24, 26 to 35, 41, 49, 55 to 60 and 86 — on 1 November 2013."
-- The day of assent is a fact: the compilation table gives 9 Nov 2011.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 2
GIVEN p IS A `Provision of Parts 1 and 2`, `the day of the Royal Assent` IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`s 2 -- the day` p `comes into operation, assent being on` `the day of the Royal Assent` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `s 1` THEN `the day of the Royal Assent`
    WHEN `s 2` THEN `the day of the Royal Assent`
    WHEN `s 5` THEN `the date` 2013 11 1
    WHEN `s 6` THEN `the date` 2013 11 1
    WHEN `s 14(1)` THEN `the date` 2013 11 1
    WHEN `s 18(1)` THEN `the date` 2013 11 1
    WHEN `s 22` THEN `the date` 2013 11 1
    WHEN `s 23` THEN `the date` 2013 11 1
    WHEN `s 24` THEN `the date` 2013 11 1
    OTHERWISE `the date` 2012 11 1

§ `Age (the encoding's reading)`

-- "has reached 6 months of age" (ss 5(1), 14(1), 18(1)), "under 6 months of age" (ss 14(3),
-- 18(3)), "a child under 18 years of age" (ss 4(1)(c), 9(2)(a)). The Act does not say how age
-- is reckoned. FORK-01, reading A (taken): age is a period beginning on the day of birth,
-- reckoned in calendar months under Interpretation Act s 62 (s 5: a year is 12 months), and
-- the age is reached on the day after that period ends -- the day numerically corresponding to
-- the birthday, or the 1st of the next month when there is no corresponding day.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 ss 5, 62; Cat Act 2011 ss 4, 5, 9, 14, 18 (FORK-01 reading A)
GIVEN `born on` IS A `Calendar date`, n IS A NUMBER, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `born on` `has reached` n `months of age on` t IF
    `the day number of` t GREATER THAN `the day number of` (`s 62 -- the last day of a period of` n `months beginning on` `born on`)

-- FORK-01, reading B: the period of age is "reckoned from" the day of birth, so under
-- Interpretation Act s 61(1)(b) the day of birth is not included.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 ss 61(1)(b), 62 (FORK-01 reading B)
GIVEN `born on` IS A `Calendar date`, n IS A NUMBER, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reading B --` `born on` `has reached` n `months of age on` t IF
    `the day number of` t GREATER THAN `the day number of` (`s 62 -- the last day of a period of` n `months beginning on` (`the day` 1 `days after` `born on`))

@ref Cat Act 2011 ss 4(1)(c), 9(2)(a)
GIVEN p IS A `Person`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE p `is a child under 18 years of age on` t IF
    NOT (p's `date of birth`) `has reached` (18 TIMES 12) `months of age on` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 ss 5(1), 14(1), 18(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE c `has reached 6 months of age on` t IF
    (c's `born on`) `has reached` 6 `months of age on` t

§ `Section 3 -- Terms used`

-- s 3(1) "cat means an animal of the species felis catus or a hybrid of that species".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "cat"
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) -- is a cat` c IF
        "an animal of the species felis catus or a hybrid of that species"
    ... c's `is an animal of the species felis catus or a hybrid of that species`

-- s 3(1) "cat management facility means — (a) a facility operated by a local government that
-- is, or may be, used for keeping cats; or (b) a facility for keeping cats that is operated by
-- a person or body prescribed; or (c) a facility for keeping cats that is operated by a person
-- or body approved in writing by a local government". (b): Cat Regulations r 4.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "cat management facility"; Cat Regulations 2012 r 4
GIVEN f IS A `Facility`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) -- is a cat management facility` f IF
        "(a)" ... f's `is operated by a local government` AND f's `is, or may be, used for keeping cats`
    ..  "(b)" ... f's `is a facility for keeping cats` AND `r 4 -- is a prescribed operator` (f's `operator`)
    ..  "(c)" ... f's `is a facility for keeping cats` AND f's `operator is approved in writing by a local government`

-- Whether the body that has custody of a cat, or receives it, is a cat management facility
-- (for Cat Regulations rr 9(2)(d) and 19).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "cat management facility"
GIVEN b IS A `Body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) -- the body is a cat management facility` b IF
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN `a facility` f THEN `s 3(1) -- is a cat management facility` f
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 3(1) "microchip means an identification device of a prescribed type that — (a) is capable
-- of being implanted in a cat; and (b) is designed to record information in a way that can be
-- electronically retrieved". Prescribed type: Cat Regulations r 5(1).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "microchip"; Cat Regulations 2012 r 5(1)
GIVEN i IS AN `Implant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) -- the device is a microchip` i IF
        "an identification device of a prescribed type" ... `r 5(1) -- the device is of the prescribed type` i
    ... "(a)" ... i's `device is capable of being implanted in a cat`
    ... "(b)" ... i's `device is designed to record information that can be electronically retrieved`

-- s 3(1) "microchip implanter means — (a) a prescribed person; or (b) a person holding the
-- prescribed qualifications for a microchip implanter". Cat Regulations r 7(1), (2).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "microchip implanter"; Cat Regulations 2012 r 7
GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) -- is a microchip implanter` p IF
        "(a)" ... `r 7(1) -- is a prescribed person` p
    ..  "(b)" ... `r 7(2) -- holds the prescribed qualifications` p

-- s 3(1) "microchipped means implanted with a microchip in a prescribed manner". Cat
-- Regulations r 8: by a microchip implanter. Status is judged at the time of implanting.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "microchipped"; Cat Regulations 2012 r 8
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) --` c `is microchipped on` t IF
    CONSIDER c's `implant`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST i THEN
            "implanted with a microchip" ... `s 3(1) -- the device is a microchip` i
        ... `the day number of` (i's `implanted on`) AT MOST `the day number of` t
        ... "in a prescribed manner" ... `r 8 -- implanted in the prescribed manner` (`s 3(1) -- is a microchip implanter` (i's `implanted by`))

-- s 3(1) "microchip database company means — (a) a person or body — (i) that keeps a microchip
-- database; and (ii) that is prescribed as a microchip database company for the purposes of
-- this definition; and (b) in relation to a particular cat, means the microchip database
-- company that keeps, or has agreed to keep, records containing information about that cat
-- and its owner". (a)(ii): Cat Regulations r 6.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "microchip database company" (a); Cat Regulations 2012 r 6
GIVEN co IS A `Database company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) -- is a microchip database company` co IF
        "(i)" ... co's `keeps a microchip database`
    ... "(ii)" ... `r 6 -- is prescribed as a microchip database company` co

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "microchip database company" (b)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) -- there is a microchip database company for` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `microchip database company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST co THEN
            `s 3(1) -- is a microchip database company` co
        ... "keeps, or has agreed to keep, records containing information about that cat and its owner"
        ... co's `keeps, or has agreed to keep, records about the cat and its owner`

GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A STRING
`the name of the microchip database company for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `microchip database company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN ""
    WHEN JUST co THEN co's `company name`

-- s 3(1) "sterilised means made permanently infertile by a surgical procedure".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "sterilised"
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) --` c `is sterilised on` t IF
    CONSIDER c's `sterilisation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST s THEN
            "made permanently infertile" ... s's `made permanently infertile`
        ... "by a surgical procedure"    ... s's `by a surgical procedure`
        ... `the day number of` (s's `performed on`) AT MOST `the day number of` t

-- s 3(1) "registered means registered under section 9"; s 9(7) and Cat Regulations r 12 give
-- the period. A cat is registered on t if any of its registrations has effect on t.
@ref Cat Act 2011 ss 3(1) "registered", 9(7); Cat Regulations 2012 r 12
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
      rs IS A LIST OF `Registration`
      t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Registration`
`the registration of` c `among` rs `having effect on` t MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `r 12(2)(a) -- the registration` r `has effect, the cat having died` (c's `has died`) `, on` t
        THEN JUST r
        ELSE `the registration of` c `among` rest `having effect on` t

GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Registration`
`the registration of` c `on` t MEANS `the registration of` c `among` (c's `registrations`) `having effect on` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "registered"
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) --` c `is registered on` t IF
    CONSIDER `the registration of` c `on` t
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST r THEN TRUE

-- s 3(1) "registered owner, in relation to a cat, means the person in whose name the cat is
-- registered".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "registered owner"
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 3(1) -- the registered owner of` c `on` t MEANS
    CONSIDER `the registration of` c `on` t
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST r THEN LIST (r's `in the name of`)

-- The local government with which the cat is registered on t (ss 5(1), 24(a), 25(a)).
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A STRING
`the local government with which` c `is registered on` t MEANS
    CONSIDER `the registration of` c `on` t
    WHEN NOTHING THEN ""
    WHEN JUST r THEN r's `with local government`

-- s 3(1) "transfer, in relation to ownership of a cat, includes — (a) sell, trade, give away,
-- take consideration for, transfer ownership of and offer for sale; and (b) to reclaim from a
-- cat management facility". Every `Kind of transfer` is one of these; "includes" leaves room
-- for others the encoding does not model.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "transfer"
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of transfer`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 3(1) -- the paragraph of "transfer" that covers` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `reclaim from a cat management facility` THEN "(b)"
    OTHERWISE "(a)"

§ `Section 4 -- Term used: owner`

-- s 4(1) "owner, in relation to a cat, means any of these persons — (a) in the case of a cat
-- that is registered, the registered owner of the cat; or (b) in the case of a cat that is not
-- registered, a person who, or an owner of a business or organisation that, ordinarily keeps
-- and cares for the cat; or (c) if a person referred to in paragraph (b) is a child under 18
-- years of age, that child's parent or guardian."
-- s 4(2) "In the case of a cat that is not registered, but is microchipped, a person whose name
-- is recorded as the owner of the cat in a microchip database is to be taken, in the absence of
-- evidence to the contrary, to be a person who ordinarily keeps and cares for the cat."
-- FORK-02, reading A (taken): "any of these persons" is cumulative, so a child who keeps the
-- cat remains an owner under (b) and the parent or guardian is an owner as well under (c).

GIVEN k IS A `Keeper`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Person`
`the persons referred to in paragraph (b) by` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual` p since THEN LIST p
    WHEN `a business or organisation` n owners since THEN owners

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `Person`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the names of` ps MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (p's `name`) FOLLOWED BY (`the names of` rest)

GIVEN ks IS A LIST OF `Keeper`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Person`
`the persons referred to in paragraph (b) among` ks MEANS
    CONSIDER ks
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN k FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `the persons` (`the persons referred to in paragraph (b) by` k) `followed by persons` (`the persons referred to in paragraph (b) among` rest)

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF `Person`
      ys IS A LIST OF `Person`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Person`
`the persons` xs `followed by persons` ys MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN ys
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x FOLLOWED BY (`the persons` rest `followed by persons` ys)

-- (c): the parents or guardians of each paragraph (b) person who is a child on t.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4(1)(c)
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `Person`
      t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 4(1)(c) -- the parents or guardians of the children among` ps `on` t MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF p `is a child under 18 years of age on` t
        THEN `the names` (p's `parents or guardians`) `followed by` (`s 4(1)(c) -- the parents or guardians of the children among` rest `on` t)
        ELSE `s 4(1)(c) -- the parents or guardians of the children among` rest `on` t

-- s 4(2): the person named in the microchip database, for an unregistered microchipped cat,
-- absent evidence to the contrary.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 4(2) -- the person taken to keep and care for` c `on` t MEANS
    IF      NOT `s 3(1) --` c `is registered on` t
        AND `s 3(1) --` c `is microchipped on` t
        AND NOT c's `there is evidence to the contrary of that record`
    THEN CONSIDER c's `name recorded as owner in a microchip database`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
         WHEN JUST n THEN LIST n
    ELSE EMPTY

-- The owners of the cat on day t, by name.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4 (FORK-02 reading A)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 4 -- the owners of` c `on` t MEANS
    IF `s 3(1) --` c `is registered on` t
    THEN `s 3(1) -- the registered owner of` c `on` t
    ELSE `the names` (`the names of` keepers) `followed by` (`the names` (`s 4(2) -- the person taken to keep and care for` c `on` t) `followed by` (`s 4(1)(c) -- the parents or guardians of the children among` keepers `on` t))
    WHERE
        keepers MEANS `the persons referred to in paragraph (b) among` (c's `keepers`)

-- FORK-02, reading B: (c) substitutes the parent or guardian for the child; the child is not
-- an owner.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4 (FORK-02 reading B)
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `Person`
      t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the names of the adults among` ps `on` t MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF p `is a child under 18 years of age on` t
        THEN `the names of the adults among` rest `on` t
        ELSE (p's `name`) FOLLOWED BY (`the names of the adults among` rest `on` t)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4 (FORK-02 reading B)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 4, reading B -- the owners of` c `on` t MEANS
    IF `s 3(1) --` c `is registered on` t
    THEN `s 3(1) -- the registered owner of` c `on` t
    ELSE `the names` (`the names of the adults among` keepers `on` t) `followed by` (`the names` (`s 4(2) -- the person taken to keep and care for` c `on` t) `followed by` (`s 4(1)(c) -- the parents or guardians of the children among` keepers `on` t))
    WHERE
        keepers MEANS `the persons referred to in paragraph (b) among` (c's `keepers`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4
GIVEN n IS A STRING, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE n `is an owner of` c `on` t IF n `is among` (`s 4 -- the owners of` c `on` t)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4 (FORK-02 reading B)
GIVEN n IS A STRING, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reading B --` n `is an owner of` c `on` t IF n `is among` (`s 4, reading B -- the owners of` c `on` t)

-- The same, asked of a person rather than a name.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` t IF
    (o's `name`) `is among` (`s 4 -- the owners of` c `on` t)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4 (FORK-02 reading B)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reading B -- the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` t IF
    (o's `name`) `is among` (`s 4, reading B -- the owners of` c `on` t)
